stateDiagram-v2
    state "pending id=1" as PENDING
    state "acknowledged id=2" as ACKNOWLEDGED
    state "refused id=3" as REFUSED
    state "expired id=4" as EXPIRED

    [*] --> PENDING: participant committed with OP stop
    PENDING --> PENDING: claim / lease renewal / transient retry
    PENDING --> ACKNOWLEDGED: HTTP 200 committed by RP
    PENDING --> REFUSED: permanent endpoint or request refusal
    PENDING --> EXPIRED: BX-10 deadline reached
    ACKNOWLEDGED --> [*]
    REFUSED --> [*]
    EXPIRED --> [*]

    note right of PENDING
        One row per grant stopped by the OP authority-stop transaction.
        Attempts and leases are delivery metadata, not lifecycle states.
        Solid Queue enqueues after commit; the recurring sweep recovers lost enqueues and leases.
        HTTP delivery runs without an OP transaction or row lock.
    end note

    note right of REFUSED
        Final refusal classes include stable endpoint misconfiguration.
        3xx responses are not followed. 413 is permanent for the fixed-size request.
    end note
